.TH elfshaker-extract 1  "extract " 
.SH NAME
elfshaker\-extract \- Can be used to extract a snapshot.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBelfshaker extract\fR [\fB\-\-reset\fR] [\fB\-\-verify\fR] [\fB\-\-force\fR] [\fB\-T\fR|\fB\-\-threads\fR] [\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsnapshot\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Can be used to extract a snapshot.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-reset\fR
Specifying this ignores the current HEAD and extract all files from the snapshot. When this flag is not specified, only an incremental file update is done.
.TP
\fB\-\-verify\fR
Enables SHA\-1 verification of the extracted files. This has a small performance overhead.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fR
Disables certain runtime checks that aim to detect unexpected file modification and prevent data loss.
.TP
\fB\-T\fR, \fB\-\-threads\fR [default: 0]
Use the specified number of worker threads for decompression. The number of threads used is proportional to the memory needed for decompression.
.TP
\fB\-\-verbose\fR
Enables verbose description of the execution process.
.TP
\fB\-\-data\-dir\fR [default: elfshaker_data]
Set the path to the elfshaker repository.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIsnapshot\fR>
The tag of the snapshot to extract.
